IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja3-sch2-second-schedule`

-- scja3-tests-sch2.l4: tests for the Second Schedule.  Expected values are written from the headings of the Schedule
-- (SCJA1969.txt lines 5716-5782) beside each assertion, and not from the module's output.

§ `Tests: the Second Schedule`

-- ---- the oath the headings allocate ----
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` Registrar) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Deputy Registrar`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Assistant Registrar`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` Interpreter) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` Sheriff) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Deputy Sheriff`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Assistant Sheriff`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` Accountant) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Commissioner for oaths`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` Clerk) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Process server`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` `Another officer of the Supreme Court`) EQUALS `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`

-- ---- seam 18: the oath taken is the appropriate oath ----
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Registrar `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` `Assistant Registrar` `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Interpreter `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Sheriff `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Clerk `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a Registrar who took the interpreter's oath, or the oath for other officers
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Registrar `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` `Deputy Registrar` `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an Interpreter is not an "other officer" for whom oath 3 is set out
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Interpreter `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Sheriff `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an oath that the Schedule does not set out
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Registrar `sch 2 another oath that the Second Schedule does not set out`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` Interpreter `sch 2 another oath that the Second Schedule does not set out`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- the words of each oath ----
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the words of the oath` `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`) EQUALS JUST "I, , having been appointed to the office of do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully discharge my judicial duties and I will do right to all manner of people after the laws and usages of the Republic of Singapore without fear or favour, affection or ill will to the best of my ability and I will be faithful and bear true allegiance to the Republic of Singapore. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of ."
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the words of the oath` `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter`) EQUALS JUST "I, , having been appointed an Interpreter of the Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully interpret, translate and transcribe from the language into the English language and from the English language into the language to the best of my knowledge, skill and ability and without fear or favour, affection or ill will. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of ."
#ASSERT (`sch 2 the words of the oath` `sch 2 another oath that the Second Schedule does not set out`) EQUALS NOTHING
